inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
typing.Hashable
\end_layout

\end_inset

 protocol.
 Every type that implements 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},breaklines=true,tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
__hash__
\end_layout

\end_inset

 has the ability to distinguish its instances and,
 besides allowing the definition of an actual 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},breaklines=true,tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
python
\end_layout

\end_inset

 set of that type as a container,
 it allows a particular (hashable) type 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},breaklines=true,tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
X
\end_layout

\end_inset

 to correspond precisely to a (classical) mathematical set 
\begin_inset Formula $X$
\end_inset

 as a type:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},breaklines=true,tabsize=4"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
class Hashable(typing.Protocol):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
	def __hash__(self) -> int:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
		...
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Hashability in 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},breaklines=true,tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
python
\end_layout

\end_inset

 perceived as discernability,
 more precisely coresponds to the notion of 
\begin_inset Formula $=$
\end_inset

 in mathematics,
 a notion used throughout here consistently,
 and is necessary when exploring mathematical foundations from a clasical perspective.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition
Given sets 
\begin_inset Formula $X$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $Y$
\end_inset

 and a function 
\begin_inset Formula $f:X\to Y$
\end_inset

:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Formula $\forall a\in X$
\end_inset

,
 the image of 
\begin_inset Formula $a$
\end_inset

 through 
\begin_inset Formula $f$
\end_inset

 is denoted 
\begin_inset Formula $f(a)$
\end_inset

,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
