\begin_layout Subsubsection
Equivalence
\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition
A 
\emph on
equivalence relation
\emph default
 
\begin_inset Formula $\sim$
\end_inset

 is a binary relation on a set 
\begin_inset Formula $X$
\end_inset

 that is:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Description
reflexive 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall a\in X$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $a\sim a$
\end_inset

,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
symmetric 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall a,b\in X$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $a\sim b$
\end_inset

 iff 
\begin_inset Formula $b\sim a$
\end_inset

,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
transitive 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall a,b,c\in X$
\end_inset

 if 
\begin_inset Formula $a\sim b$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $b\sim c$
\end_inset

 then 
\begin_inset Formula $a\sim c$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Standard
Every equivalence relation 
\begin_inset Formula $\sim$
\end_inset

 corresponds its nonequivalence counterpart 
\begin_inset Formula $\nsim$
\end_inset

 as
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\nsim:X\times X\to\{0,1\}:x,y\mapsto x\nsim y=\neg(x\sim y),
\]

\end_inset

and vice versa.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Unlike equality (hashability),
 equivalence relations may introduce a sort of bucketting of instances in 
\begin_inset Formula $X$
\end_inset

,
 which is why in 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},breaklines=true,tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
python
\end_layout

\end_inset

 they correspond to distinct from 
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},breaklines=true,tabsize=4"
inline true
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
__hash__
\end_layout

\end_inset

 methods:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "language=Python,fontfamily=tt,fontsize={\scriptsize},breaklines=true,tabsize=4"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
class Equivalence(typing.Hashable):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
	def __eq__(self,
 other:
 X) -> bool:
 return not self != other
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
	def __ne__(self,
 other:
 X) -> bool:
 return not self == other
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
